      "message": "@wescande@google.com\n\nSorry to let you misunderstand something. I added the comment. I\u0027ll keep it simple and add the real case in the code and leave for background information  right here.\n\n---\n\nThe main idea is to try to fallback the active device when the active device is null. Somehow the current logic only covers this case when [disconnecting](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/ActiveDeviceManager.java;l\u003d503;drc\u003da4e7e0113226fab235b0bb6a81f4d2c21efd6e21?q\u003dsetFallbackDeviceActiveLocked\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fgoogleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain).\n\nHowever, there\u0027s a case that remote device is connected but HFP Service or other application remove the HFP active device. So we also need to try to fallback to another active device. \n\nSo I added this cl. aosp/3324694\n\n---\n\n[This cl]\nI didn\u0027t consider the le broadcast case. This is kinda like a special case to me. It\u0027ll set the active device to null when broadcasting. If in this moment we fallback to another active device, we might break the audio routing logic.\n\nSo I make this change for this case.",
